🔥 QUESTION 2: DISJOINT SET (UNION–FIND)

👉 Extremely important for Graph problems, Cycle detection, Connected components, MST (Kruskal’s Algorithm)

1️⃣ Problem Statement

Design a Disjoint Set (Union–Find) data structure that supports:

find(x) → Finds the ultimate parent of x

union(x, y) → Connects two elements

Efficient operations using:

Path Compression

Union by Rank

Example Problem
n = 5
Union(0, 1)
Union(1, 2)
Union(3, 4)

Find(2) → 0
Find(4) → 3
Are 2 and 4 connected? → No

2️⃣ Key Idea 💡

Disjoint Set:

Keeps track of groups

Each group has one leader (parent)

Two optimizations:

Path Compression → makes find fast

Union by Rank → keeps tree shallow

3️⃣ Data Structures Used

parent[] → stores parent of each node

rank[] → approximate depth of tree

4️⃣ Algorithm
➤ Initialize

Each node is its own parent

Rank = 0

➤ Find (with Path Compression)

If node is its own parent → return it

Else:

Recursively find parent

Attach directly to root

➤ Union (by Rank)

Find root of both elements

Attach smaller depth tree under larger

If equal, increase rank

5️⃣ Java Code (Interview-Ready)
class DisjointSet {

    int[] parent;
    int[] rank;

    // Step 1: Constructor
    public DisjointSet(int n) {
        parent = new int[n];
        rank = new int[n];

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            parent[i] = i; // each node is its own parent
            rank[i] = 0;
        }
    }

    // Step 2: Find with Path Compression
    public int find(int node) {
        if (parent[node] != node) {
            parent[node] = find(parent[node]); 
        }
        return parent[node];
    }

    // Step 3: Union by Rank
    public void union(int u, int v) {

        int parentU = find(u);
        int parentV = find(v);

        if (parentU == parentV) {
            return; // already in same set
        }

        if (rank[parentU] < rank[parentV]) {
            parent[parentU] = parentV;
        } 
        else if (rank[parentU] > rank[parentV]) {
            parent[parentV] = parentU;
        } 
        else {
            parent[parentV] = parentU;
            rank[parentU]++;
        }
    }
}

6️⃣ Line-by-Line Explanation 🔍
🔹 parent and rank arrays
int[] parent;
int[] rank;


parent[i] → leader of node i

rank[i] → depth of tree

🔹 Constructor
parent[i] = i;
rank[i] = 0;


👉 Every node starts as independent set

🔹 Find Method
if (parent[node] != node)


👉 Node is not root

parent[node] = find(parent[node]);


👉 Path compression

Flattens structure

Makes future calls faster

🔹 Union Method
int parentU = find(u);
int parentV = find(v);


👉 Find leaders

if (parentU == parentV) return;


👉 Cycle prevention

rank[parentU] < rank[parentV]


👉 Attach smaller depth tree under larger

rank[parentU]++;


👉 Increase rank when equal height trees merge

